{"availability":"available","full":"FSoft-AI4Code/CodeWiki","name":"CodeWiki","description":"[ACL 2026] Open-source framework for holistic, structured repository-level documentation across multilingual codebases","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":1783,"forks":268,"created":"2025-06-25T09:48:13Z","updated":"2026-10-15T12:55:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fsoft-ai4code.github.io/CodeWiki/","topics":["automated-documentation","code-documentation","code-understanding","documentation-generator","open-source-deepwiki","repository-documentation"],"demo":"https://fsoft-ai4code.github.io/codewiki-demo/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:00:37.953Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:00:37.953Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:00:37.953Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:17.935Z","stars":1754,"forks":266},{"at":"2026-10-07T23:29:15.956Z","stars":1757,"forks":267},{"at":"2026-10-10T01:07:29.729Z","stars":1760,"forks":266},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:00:37.953Z","stars":1783,"forks":268}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Repository-level documentation for large codebases, written by AI agents from the dependency graph.","Quick start • What's new in 2.0 • Features • Benchmark • Guides • Paper","📚 CodeWiki documents itself. Browse the documentation it generated for this repository at CodeWiki docs."],"features":["Languages. Python, Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, C, C++, C#, Kotlin, PHP, Ruby, Scala, Rust, Dart (Flutter-aware).","Hierarchical decomposition. The dependency graph is clustered into a module tree, recursively, so a 1.4M-line repository gets the same treatment as a 10k-line one. Depth and size thresholds are configurable.","Recursive agents. One agent per leaf module reads the code through tools and writes the page. Parent pages are written from child pages. Diagrams are validated before they are saved.","Incremental updates. --update refreshes only what changed. --compare-to sets the base commit for CI and squashed merges. If too much changed, it falls back to a full build and says so.","--language takes a code or a name (ja, Japanese, vi, zh, ...). Page text, headings and diagram labels follow it. Filenames and module names stay ASCII so links keep working, and the viewer shows the translated page…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FSoft-AI4Code/CodeWiki/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1ac92d4b053751aab148031bf817b321432e1fd64dfac904c784ed8127965184","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T09:49:42.774Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:49:42.774Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Repository-level documentation for large codebases, written by AI agents from the dependency graph.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FSoft-AI4Code/CodeWiki/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"It needs an LLM API key, or a Claude or Codex subscription, or an AI IDE that speaks MCP.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FSoft-AI4Code/CodeWiki/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"It needs an LLM API key, or a Claude or Codex subscription, or an AI IDE that speaks MCP.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FSoft-AI4Code/CodeWiki/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Pages mirror the module tree: a module's page sits next to the folder holding its sub-modules (auth.md, auth/login.md). --flat puts every page in ./docs instead, which helps small models that get relative links wrong. --update keeps the layout the docs were generated with.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FSoft-AI4Code/CodeWiki/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"1ac92d4b053751aab148031bf817b321432e1fd64dfac904c784ed8127965184","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FSoft-AI4Code/CodeWiki/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T09:49:42.775Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T07:13:16Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"h